sites.stub:
Trampoline C5_Tramp = '55 8b ec 51 57 e9 <rel32 -> 0x67BDC5>'. The displaced prologue contains no relative operands. At 0x67BDC5 'mov edi,ecx' needs ECX=this, which the thiscall into the trampoline provides.

Wrapper, a C++ call-boundary stub at a function entry:
  bool __fastcall C5_CalcPhysicsXform(Drawable* d /*ECX*/, void* /*EDX*/, float* out /*[esp+4], 16 bytes*/)
  ; fastcall pops 4, which equals the original 'ret 4'
  using T = bool(__thiscall*)(void*, float*);  T orig = C5_Tramp;
  if (!g_m60 || __readfsdword(0x24) != g_mainTid) return orig(d,out);   // 30 mode and other threads: exactly stock
  char* obj  = *(char**)((char*)d+0xFC);  char* ai = obj ? *(char**)(obj+0x260) : 0;
  char* loco = ai ? *(char**)(ai+0x1F0) : 0;          // the same chain as 0x67BDC7..0x67BDE8 and 0x68B31D
  if (!g_inB) {                                        // A-render = stock render k
     bool r = orig(d,out);
     if (r && loco) C5_store(loco, d, *(uint32_t*)(loco+0xAC) /*just stamped = m_frame*/, g_renderId, out /*16 bytes*/);
     return r; }
  // B-render: NEVER call orig. Its only possible effects would be to run an integrator and stamp loco+0xAC, which mutates persistent state.
  if (!loco) return false;                             // orig returns 0 here too
  C5Entry* e = C5_find(loco);
  if (e && e->drw==d && e->renderIdA==g_renderId-1 && e->frame==*(uint32_t*)(loco+0xAC) && e->replayId!=g_renderId) {
     memcpy(out, e->out, 16); e->replayId = g_renderId; return true; }  // = stock render k's first call for this loco
  if (*(uint32_t*)(loco+0xAC) != GC->m_frame) ++g_tmC5Suppressed;     // drawable not drawn on A; stock k did not step it either
  return false;                                        // = stock k's later calls, or k produced nothing (paused, unsupported appearance)

Table: open addressing, 4096 slots, hash = ((uintptr)loco>>3)*0x9E3779B1>>20, probe up to 8 slots. On store, reuse the slot with the same loco or one with renderIdA != g_renderId; if none is free, drop and count g_tmC5Drop. A drop is visual only: that unit shows no pitch/roll on one B frame. Entries are self-invalidating through renderIdA, so a flush on mode switch or reset is optional (the PLAN asks for one; a memset is fine).
